    VOCABULARY  k9+ - k6   -15.2 +/-  5.7 Hz (2.7 SE)  <- nine words vs six,
                                                      trials/word MATCHED
    levels the F1 reach holds at k9+:  span 18.7 Hz / 2 x scatter 44.8  ->  1.2 levels

  THE SCORE IS GEOMETRY. At every k the creature's per-axis accuracy is
  within 2 SE of what its own DELIVERED spacing and scatter predict, so
  the falling excess is not a readout failure and `nearest` is behaving.
  The question is what shrinks the DELIVERY, and F1 answers it cleanly
  because its demand is 59 Hz in all three arms.

  VOCABULARY IS THE COST, NOT THE TEACHING BUDGET. With trials per word
  MATCHED, nine words deliver -15.2 +/- 5.7 Hz of F1 separation against
  six (2.7 SE) while 1.5x the teaching bought only +3.3 +/- 4.4. The
  words INTERFERE: each one added costs the others reach, and at k=9 the
  delivered span holds ~1.2 distinguishable levels. This is a capacity
  limit proper -- on the REACH the bias can build, which is where
  ctxscale's ~118 Hz asymptote and ceiling-is-an-exponent already put it.
